W=1400 H=1090
TITLE=Who reads your robots.txt
DESC=Your robots.txt file, at yourbusiness.com/robots.txt, is read by two groups of crawlers, the programs search engines and AI tools use to read websites. Search crawlers: let these in, so your website can appear in search results and AI answers. Googlebot for Google Search, AI Overviews and AI Mode. Bingbot for Bing and Microsoft Copilot. OAI-SearchBot for ChatGPT search. Claude-SearchBot for Claude search, and Claude-User for Claude fetching a page on demand when a user asks. PerplexityBot for Perplexity. Training crawlers: your choice, because blocking these does not remove you from search answers. GPTBot for OpenAI's AI models, ClaudeBot for Anthropic's AI models and Google-Extended for Google's Gemini. Blocking Google-Extended does not affect Google Search. If you have no robots.txt, every crawler is allowed. A wrong rule can keep all of them out, and the prompt in step 3 lets the right ones in while keeping private pages blocked.
---
  <text x="50" y="84" class="display" font-size="36" font-weight="700">Who reads your robots.txt</text>
  <text x="50" y="124" class="copy muted" font-size="22">Crawlers are the programs search engines and AI tools use to read websites.</text>

  <g filter="url(#card-shadow)">
    <rect x="450" y="168" width="500" height="92" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#080809" stroke-width="3"/>
  </g>
  <text x="482" y="204" class="mini">YOUR FILE</text>
  <text x="482" y="240" class="code" font-size="21" font-weight="700">yourbusiness.com/robots.txt</text>
